<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, soyoil prices up, soymeal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, soyoil prices up, soymeal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices climbed 100 to 200 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on good demand from processing plants on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also firm on limited supply from processing plants and refineries and good local demand. Soyoil solvent was up by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 400 rupees per tonne today.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on limited export demand at the higher price level. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $130-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550 rupees per tonne FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
